    "narrative": "The focal point of today\u2019s lineup is the elite utility of **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. Facing a favorable matchup against Peralta, the combination of a high-ceiling park factor (+16%) and his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching makes him our must-start anchor. Alongside him, **Kyle Tucker** (75.04) and **Andy Pages** (72.93) are top-tier plays. Both benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Bubba Chandler, whose underlying metrics suggest a vulnerable outing. We are prioritizing these three heavily, specifically leveraging the slow delivery of the opposing staff to boost our stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our Roto standing.\n\nWhile we are confident in our outfield depth, the volatility of the lower end of the lineup is notable. **Luis Robert Jr.** (42.17) is barely clearing our 40-point threshold, hampered by a rigid platoon disadvantage and an ominous 37% rain risk, mirroring the situational concern for **Miguel Vargas** (49.51). **Coby Mayo** (56.02) remains our most viable UTIL play; he projects significantly better than **Dominic Smith** (38.13), who fell short of our floor due to a brutal matchup against the elite arm of Misiorowski (2.09 xERA). The decision to bench **Dominic Smith** was straightforward: while he offered a minor platoon boost, he could not overcome the SP skill deficit that keeps his ceiling firmly capped today.\n\nRisk management remains paramount as we navigate a slate with two weather-sensitive targets. **Miguel Vargas** and **Luis Robert Jr.** are officially flagged for potential rain delays; should these games be postponed, we will need to pivot to our bench assets. While **Jordan Westburg** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remain sidelined on the IL, their absence continues to compress our rotation, forcing players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Liam Hicks** into active roles to chase volume. We will monitor lineup changes for **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** closely, as any shift downward in the batting order would necessitate a recalibration of our current 5x5 projections.",
